\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Left-biased version of `List.zipWith`. `zipWithLeft' f as bs` applies `f` to each\npair of elements `aᵢ ∈ as` and `bᵢ ∈ bs`. If `bs` is shorter than `as`, `f` is\napplied to `none` for the remaining `aᵢ`. Returns the results of the `f`\napplications and the remaining `bs`.\n```\nzipWithLeft' prod.mk [1, 2] ['a'] = ([(1, some 'a'), (2, none)], [])\nzipWithLeft' prod.mk [1] ['a', 'b'] = ([(1, some 'a')], ['b'])\n```\n","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/List/Basic.html#List.zipWithLeft'","kind":"def","line":706,"name":"List.zipWithLeft'","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/3a067208130fab4154e6a4dd29efd07e3a9466bd/Batteries/Data/List/Basic.lean#L706-L719"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/List/Basic.html#List.dropSlice_eq_dropSliceTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">dropSlice_eq_dropSliceTR</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\">@<a href=\"./Batteries/Data/List/Basic.html#List.dropSlice\">dropSlice</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> @<a href=\"./Batteries/Data/List/Basic.html#List.dropSliceTR\">dropSliceTR</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","d